To construct these metrics, we used the proportion PC of actions to be carried out, based on model predictions:
1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$  P_C = \frac{ \text{FP} + \text{TP} }{N}, $$\end{document}PC=FP+TPN,where FP and TP are the number of false and true positives, respectively (analogously for FN and TN); and N = FP + TP + FN + TN is the total number of appointments (for the specialty). This quantity can be seen as a proxy of the cost of actions taken to prevent no-shows.

The second quantity used to define our custom metrics is the proportion PR of no-show reduction, obtained from model predictions. First, let NSPi be the existing no-show rate, and NSPf be the no-show rate obtained after considering that all TP cases attend their appointment. That is:
2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
